1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,960
You guys really need to stop this nonsense.

2
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,740
Today is the Tokyo Metropolis League.

3
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:10,660
The first game for the B-Team.

4
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:12,640
What's with you all this week?

5
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:15,600
This negativity is really killing your team's morale.

6
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:19,840
Honestly, you're not competing against some world-class opponent out here.

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,460
This should be low-hanging fruit, but we're barely going to get by.

8
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:24,780
And why?

9
00:01:59,034 --> 00:02:05,034
Have you noticed that ever since that whole thing went down with Asari, the rest of the first years are feeling it too?

10
00:02:05,034 --> 00:02:09,034
I mean, he's like criminal crazy man. I didn't think he'd be that pissed.

11
00:02:09,034 --> 00:02:12,034
It's like all his hair fell out when they made Ashito a starter.

12
00:02:12,034 --> 00:02:15,034
You stole their spot!

13
00:02:15,034 --> 00:02:19,034
Talk about nuts. But I admit I'm obsessed with what he said.

14
00:02:19,034 --> 00:02:26,034
Yeah, I feel you, bro. This sucks. How are we supposed to play at our best feeling like this?

15
00:02:26,034 --> 00:02:31,034
And right now you're wondering, why were Kurada and Asari mad at you?

16
00:02:31,034 --> 00:02:34,034
Find the answer to that question.

17
00:02:34,034 --> 00:02:38,034
If you can't do that, I won't field you in a match for the next three months.

18
00:02:38,034 --> 00:02:41,034
So act as if your life depends on it.

19
00:02:41,034 --> 00:02:48,034
I'm afraid I don't have the answers yet, coach. Sorry. My only priority right now is this game.

20
00:02:48,034 --> 00:02:53,034
Okay, dry your eyes. I told you I'll be home at some point.

21
00:02:53,034 --> 00:02:59,034
When? How am I supposed to know that? But I'll see you then. You just don't stop, do you? What are you, my mother now?

22
00:02:59,034 --> 00:03:02,034
Hey, old man! Sorry! Manager Fukuda?

23
00:03:02,034 --> 00:03:04,034
Yeah? What do you want?

24
00:03:04,034 --> 00:03:06,034
Is that... Hana?

25
00:03:06,034 --> 00:03:12,034
Yeah. That's weird. How'd you know? Wait a minute. You're not seeing her, are you?

26
00:03:12,034 --> 00:03:19,034
Can you hold up your receiver really quick? My receiver? You mean my cell phone?

27
00:03:19,034 --> 00:03:29,034
Hey! I just wanna say I'm doing your meal plan. And? I'm off to play in my first match and they made me a starter, isn't that cool?

28
00:03:29,034 --> 00:03:34,034
Yeah! My official debut is as the reincarnation of Farence Puskas!

29
00:03:34,034 --> 00:03:37,034
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

30
00:03:37,034 --> 00:03:42,034
So if you wanna come cheer for me, you can. That's all.

31
00:03:42,034 --> 00:03:55,034
Uh... Ashito. You think you can win? How do you feel?

32
00:03:55,034 --> 00:04:00,034
I've never had to think this much about a game before. But we'll win.

33
00:04:00,034 --> 00:04:03,034
Yeah? How do you figure?

34
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:05,034
Cause I'm gonna score for us.

35
00:04:05,034 --> 00:04:15,034
I love to be the one to point out the obvious, but... Soccer is what we call a team sport. You can't do anything alone.

36
00:04:15,034 --> 00:04:21,034
That's what makes it fun. That's what it's all about.

37
00:04:21,034 --> 00:04:28,034
What the? Is Spurion Youth Team B?

38
00:04:28,034 --> 00:04:40,034
B? No way! There can't be two teams! What am I supposed to do? I was told to photograph the future national team! How do I know which one that is if the teams are split in two? Mr. Sekio is going to kill me!

39
00:04:40,034 --> 00:04:43,034
Let's go, Sekio! Let's go, Sekio!

40
00:04:43,034 --> 00:04:53,034
Hmm, so this is the opponent's side. No flashy cheer teams, like at high school level. And no one following, so they're easy to spot, which is cool. So they must be...

41
00:04:53,034 --> 00:04:55,034
Yep, called it!

42
00:04:57,034 --> 00:05:06,034
Oh, by the way, did you mean what you said earlier? Are there actually good players on this team? Do you just know a lot about a Spurion, or what?

43
00:05:06,034 --> 00:05:14,034
Uh, okay. Sorry, you seemed like a nice person who might have some answers. But we all know looks can be deceiving.

44
00:05:14,034 --> 00:05:19,034
I get that they're the B team, but aren't they supposed to be elite players? They kind of low.

45
00:05:19,034 --> 00:05:21,034
Yeah, what a joke.

46
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:31,034
The hell, Takashima? What is your problem? I was trying to pass it to the front, dude!

47
00:05:31,034 --> 00:05:34,034
Seriously? No one's coming to follow up?

48
00:05:36,034 --> 00:05:38,034
Left side, watch out!

49
00:05:44,034 --> 00:05:47,034
How did every single one of you what sound like that?

50
00:05:49,034 --> 00:05:50,034
Nice goal!

51
00:05:51,034 --> 00:05:52,034
Bunch of idiots!

52
00:05:52,034 --> 00:06:04,034
35 minutes into the first half? It's zero to three?

53
00:06:04,034 --> 00:06:14,034
What was that besides pathetic? We may be the B team, but we are still wearing the Asperion uniform. Step it up!

54
00:06:14,034 --> 00:06:16,034
We did everything we were supposed to.

55
00:06:19,034 --> 00:06:24,034
Please enlighten me. When you use the pronoun, we, who exactly are you referring to, Aseri?

56
00:06:24,034 --> 00:06:31,034
Everyone in this room was off their game today, including you, Princess, so stop being so desperate to blame the tryout players!

57
00:06:31,034 --> 00:06:33,034
That's not what I'm doing. Cut it out!

58
00:06:33,034 --> 00:06:40,034
I'm so disappointed in all of you. You brought your childish issues from practice right into the game.

59
00:06:40,034 --> 00:06:47,034
It's humiliating to see you be so careless and give up three goals. You're wasting your talent by acting like babies!

60
00:06:47,034 --> 00:06:50,034
Didn't you come here because you want to be professional players?

61
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:54,034
There was not one hair on your skin that could claim an atom of professionalism.

62
00:06:55,034 --> 00:06:58,034
Maybe because I still have no clue how to figure out this stupid assignment.

63
00:06:59,034 --> 00:07:02,034
First half, I tried defense and that was frickin' boring.

64
00:07:02,034 --> 00:07:06,034
I also tried less dribbling and more passing so that no one would cry about not touching the ball.

65
00:07:07,034 --> 00:07:11,034
Even though I was bored to tears. I'm so over the sharing as caring baby soccer.

66
00:07:12,034 --> 00:07:18,034
Well, that's the price to pay when you're a genius. You can do anything and everything. They all want a piece.

67
00:07:18,034 --> 00:07:25,034
Except those punk asses. It's like they don't even want the win. They're just sitting there pouting.

68
00:07:26,034 --> 00:07:30,034
I know they see me, but they won't even look up at me. It's so frickin' dramatic.

69
00:07:30,034 --> 00:07:36,034
Just look at me, you jerks! Don't you get it? If we can't all work together, we don't stand a chance at winning.

70
00:07:37,034 --> 00:07:39,034
Isn't that why we're here? To play at our very best?

71
00:07:41,034 --> 00:07:45,034
Coach Nozomi, almost all of them are done. Bring in some of the second and third years.

72
00:07:45,034 --> 00:07:46,034
What?

73
00:07:46,034 --> 00:07:54,034
We can't make a play with this crap. Did you see them? Aoi, Kurara, and Asari? They're useless. Like they're drunk or sleepwalking.

74
00:07:54,034 --> 00:08:02,034
And yeah, I realize I'm overstepping quite a bit. Forgive me, but I don't want us to lose here.

75
00:08:03,034 --> 00:08:07,034
I agree with you. So act as if your life depends on it.

76
00:08:08,034 --> 00:08:09,034
Hold on.

77
00:08:09,034 --> 00:08:13,034
Togashi. For the second half, you'll go in for Ishiki at center back.

78
00:08:15,034 --> 00:08:20,034
Coach, I don't think you really mean that. Why would you add Togashi to the mix when the goal is to clean up the mess?

79
00:08:20,034 --> 00:08:27,034
I'm confused by it myself. I don't see how I can score three goals with these entitled pouty players.

80
00:08:28,034 --> 00:08:34,034
They're more about protecting their elite status and cheap sense of pride over playing with real skill and winning.

81
00:08:35,034 --> 00:08:39,034
Guess that's how it is when you're from the academy. Not much ever changes, I see.

82
00:08:39,034 --> 00:08:44,034
Bastard! Say it one more time! Togashi!

83
00:08:46,034 --> 00:08:48,034
That's not true, okay?

84
00:08:49,034 --> 00:08:50,034
What?

85
00:08:51,034 --> 00:08:59,034
I don't mean about us not being in sync. We weren't, and we aren't communicating. But something is happening, and you need to see it.

86
00:09:00,034 --> 00:09:07,034
Everyone here is doing their best. None of us are stupid enough to put ourselves through all this if we didn't want to win.

87
00:09:07,034 --> 00:09:10,034
Nothing matters more. We know that.

88
00:09:14,034 --> 00:09:16,034
Clean up whatever's festering.

89
00:09:18,034 --> 00:09:24,034
I'm not giving you any more matches. This is your only shot. There are 45 minutes left in the match.

90
00:09:25,034 --> 00:09:29,034
Get comfortable with being uncomfortable out on the field. Hard work is exhausting.

91
00:09:29,034 --> 00:09:37,034
If you all self-destruct, at least you'll know you gave it everything you had. Then you'll do training runs until summer.

92
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:47,034
Thank you.

93
00:09:47,034 --> 00:10:05,034
What? Are you freaking kidding me? They've got four, five, six defenders back there. The halfbacks are mostly positioned as defenders as well. I never thought they'd dare fall back that much.

94
00:10:05,034 --> 00:10:08,034
Well, they're focusing on defense, not appearances.

95
00:10:08,034 --> 00:10:11,034
That's right! Let's finish this out! You're gonna crush them!

96
00:10:12,034 --> 00:10:14,034
B-team? More like D-team!

97
00:10:14,034 --> 00:10:26,034
Aoi, Kurada, Asari. What's going through your heads? Better figure it out quickly. If you guys don't get your useless line together, they'll bust through and we'll be screwed.

98
00:10:26,034 --> 00:10:34,034
Huh? What is he talking about? Line? Why did only those two get so upset?

99
00:10:35,034 --> 00:10:46,034
Wait a minute. Is that it? I did notice that the three of us were always playing on the same line. I don't remember any other players there. Was it a test?

100
00:10:46,034 --> 00:10:57,034
What's happening? I don't feel right. Something is seriously strange here. But, what?

101
00:10:57,034 --> 00:11:15,034
What an odd level of defense.

102
00:11:15,034 --> 00:11:23,034
But it seems to be working out for them just fine. And it's not like they have anyone who can bust it open. Can't expect much else from a B-team.

103
00:11:27,034 --> 00:11:33,034
What? Are you kidding me? I didn't touch him!

104
00:11:34,034 --> 00:11:41,034
I suggest you watch your mouth, kid. Calm down. You're getting desperate and it shows. Keep it up and I'll give you a yellow card.

105
00:11:43,034 --> 00:11:49,034
What's your deal? Anything to say? Aren't you embarrassed? Why are you playing scared defense?

106
00:11:50,034 --> 00:11:54,034
We're getting bored. Wake up. Give us a challenge.

107
00:11:54,034 --> 00:11:59,034
Hmm. Yeah, I agree it's not fun. But hey, you know why it's necessary?

108
00:12:00,034 --> 00:12:05,034
Deal with it! We refuse to be defeated by a consolation prize team!

109
00:12:05,034 --> 00:12:06,034
Hmm.

110
00:12:06,034 --> 00:12:07,034
Hmm.

111
00:12:11,034 --> 00:12:17,034
Say something, cause you look creepy.

112
00:12:17,034 --> 00:12:24,034
I noticed something. You've been overlapping. And you're incredible. Like, you're a master at it.

113
00:12:24,034 --> 00:12:25,034
Hmm?

114
00:12:25,034 --> 00:12:36,034
You've always been a defender, haven't you? I just saw you come back from the keeper's area. Holy crap, I'm right! Whenever I look back, I always see you behind me somehow.

115
00:12:36,034 --> 00:12:37,034
Hmm.

116
00:12:37,034 --> 00:12:38,034
Hmm.

117
00:12:38,034 --> 00:12:40,034
Hey! Everyone come back!

118
00:12:42,034 --> 00:12:45,034
And... and Kurada, he does it too.

119
00:12:47,034 --> 00:12:53,034
I see it. He always positions himself between me and Asuri. Hey guys, what's up?

120
00:12:53,034 --> 00:13:00,034
Why don't you tell me? Were you leisurely watching your teammates this whole time? We only have 30 minutes!

121
00:13:00,034 --> 00:13:06,034
I see it! Notice right away! As soon as I paid attention, I knew what they were doing! It's obvious!

122
00:13:06,034 --> 00:13:12,034
Well, it should be. All three of you are sharing the same line. It doesn't take a genius to notice your surroundings.

123
00:13:13,034 --> 00:13:17,034
No, that's not it! Not all of it! But even if it was...

124
00:13:18,034 --> 00:13:19,034
Uh...

125
00:13:22,034 --> 00:13:25,034
Think you can act human for at least 15 minutes?

126
00:13:26,034 --> 00:13:28,034
I don't know, to be honest. I'm weirded out.

127
00:13:29,034 --> 00:13:30,034
Huh?

128
00:13:31,034 --> 00:13:33,034
This entire time, I've been thinking...

129
00:13:34,034 --> 00:13:36,034
Why aren't they getting the play that I'm trying to make?

130
00:13:37,034 --> 00:13:38,034
What am I doing wrong?

131
00:13:39,034 --> 00:13:41,034
Why are they doing their best to ignore me out here?

132
00:13:42,034 --> 00:13:43,034
But now...

133
00:13:44,034 --> 00:13:47,034
I see that I was the one ignoring what was right in front of my eyes!

134
00:13:49,034 --> 00:13:52,034
Was it me? Was I the source of the problem?

135
00:13:53,034 --> 00:13:55,034
Hey, Nozomi, let's swish him out.

136
00:13:56,034 --> 00:13:58,034
If we don't, it could affect the morale in the future.

137
00:13:58,034 --> 00:14:02,034
I feel like we especially need to call back Aoi and Asari.

138
00:14:04,034 --> 00:14:05,034
Five more minutes.

139
00:14:06,034 --> 00:14:08,034
I need a little more time to watch them.

140
00:14:09,034 --> 00:14:13,034
Asari! Returning to center! It's surrounding you! Asari!

141
00:14:14,034 --> 00:14:16,034
That's right. Distance.

142
00:14:17,034 --> 00:14:20,034
The three of us tend to be within proximity of each other most of the time.

143
00:14:20,034 --> 00:14:29,034
If I take the ball and run with it, without ever looking around, they usually try to catch up with me.

144
00:14:30,034 --> 00:14:34,034
But still, I can't quite make sense of what that means yet.

145
00:14:34,034 --> 00:14:40,034
Okay. So, Kuroda is over there right now. And I'm out here, but...

146
00:14:41,034 --> 00:14:44,034
If I were in Asari's place, where would I most want me to be?

147
00:14:44,034 --> 00:14:47,034
Whoa! It went through!

148
00:14:48,034 --> 00:14:50,034
Hey, Aoi! Go cover!

149
00:14:50,034 --> 00:14:51,034
Yeah! Goal kick!

150
00:14:51,034 --> 00:14:53,034
Too bad, you team! You finally got through and nobody cares!

151
00:14:54,034 --> 00:14:55,034
Don't get used to it! You got lucky!

152
00:14:56,034 --> 00:14:57,034
Oh!

153
00:14:58,034 --> 00:14:59,034
Oh!

154
00:14:59,034 --> 00:15:00,034
Oh!

155
00:15:00,034 --> 00:15:03,034
Hey, Owie! Go cover!

156
00:15:06,034 --> 00:15:08,034
Yeah! Goal kick!

157
00:15:09,034 --> 00:15:11,034
Aw, too bad, youth team.

158
00:15:11,034 --> 00:15:13,034
You finally got through, and nobody cares!

159
00:15:13,034 --> 00:15:16,034
Don't get used to it! You got lucky!

160
00:15:24,034 --> 00:15:26,034
Another classic Owie moment.

161
00:15:26,034 --> 00:15:29,034
The ball had gone through nice and clean,

162
00:15:29,034 --> 00:15:32,034
but he just stood there staring at it, doing nothing.

163
00:15:34,034 --> 00:15:36,034
He performed like this all day,

164
00:15:36,034 --> 00:15:38,034
and it's already been five minutes.

165
00:15:38,034 --> 00:15:39,034
Let's pull him.

166
00:15:39,034 --> 00:15:42,034
I'm more disappointed in your performance.

167
00:15:42,034 --> 00:15:45,034
You're always saying to think outside the theory,

168
00:15:45,034 --> 00:15:48,034
but I can see it never really applied to you.

169
00:15:48,034 --> 00:15:50,034
You say you're a hardcore Fukuda fanatic,

170
00:15:50,034 --> 00:15:54,034
but you're clearly rattled by our opponents being up by three goals.

171
00:15:54,034 --> 00:15:59,034
We have thirty more minutes to go.

172
00:15:59,034 --> 00:16:00,034
Plenty of time.

173
00:16:00,034 --> 00:16:03,034
I'm still expecting something exciting to happen.

174
00:16:03,034 --> 00:16:05,034
Maybe you should expect the same.

175
00:16:05,034 --> 00:16:08,034
I can't believe it.

176
00:16:08,034 --> 00:16:14,034
I actually got my hopes up for you again.

177
00:16:14,034 --> 00:16:17,034
Nice move on the defensive positioning,

178
00:16:17,034 --> 00:16:20,034
and a one-touch pass to Fukuda was brilliant.

179
00:16:20,034 --> 00:16:21,034
I fell for it.

180
00:16:21,034 --> 00:16:24,034
But then you couldn't be bothered to go into cover.

181
00:16:24,034 --> 00:16:27,034
You obviously still don't get what this game's about.

182
00:16:28,034 --> 00:16:29,034
Stupid.

183
00:16:29,034 --> 00:16:32,034
I don't know how a noob like you ended up on Asperion

184
00:16:32,034 --> 00:16:34,034
when you clearly don't know what you're doing.

185
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:36,034
You won't be able to fake it forever.

186
00:16:36,034 --> 00:16:37,034
Oh?

187
00:16:37,034 --> 00:16:38,034
Asuri!

188
00:16:38,034 --> 00:16:52,034
The three of them are interesting to watch.

189
00:16:52,034 --> 00:16:55,034
Those three that play the left wing?

190
00:16:55,034 --> 00:17:00,034
Oh, come on!

191
00:17:00,034 --> 00:17:03,034
You ladies just gonna keep passing the ball between the three of you?

192
00:17:03,034 --> 00:17:06,034
Why are you wasting time when we're up three on you?

193
00:17:06,034 --> 00:17:08,034
Oh, I get it.

194
00:17:08,034 --> 00:17:11,034
So one of those players is actually your boyfriend, is that right?

195
00:17:11,034 --> 00:17:14,034
If it's the cute one with the blonde hair, you're my new hero!

196
00:17:16,034 --> 00:17:18,034
Not even close, but it's hard to explain.

197
00:17:19,034 --> 00:17:21,034
Something's changed between those three,

198
00:17:21,034 --> 00:17:24,034
and it happened so quickly.

199
00:17:24,034 --> 00:17:26,034
Sorry, Kurada.

200
00:17:26,034 --> 00:17:27,034
I suck.

201
00:17:27,034 --> 00:17:30,034
I was so obsessed with how stupid Asuri was feeling,

202
00:17:30,034 --> 00:17:32,034
I completely tuned you out.

203
00:17:33,034 --> 00:17:34,034
Pass the ball,

204
00:17:34,034 --> 00:17:37,034
and then immediately go to cover the receiver.

205
00:17:37,034 --> 00:17:38,034
Do I have that right?

206
00:17:42,034 --> 00:17:44,034
You're passing the ball to him again?

207
00:17:45,034 --> 00:17:47,034
So if I were Kurada,

208
00:17:47,034 --> 00:17:49,034
where would I position myself?

209
00:17:51,034 --> 00:17:53,034
Ashito! Go to the other side!

210
00:17:53,034 --> 00:17:56,034
Ashito! Behind you! Pass it back!

211
00:17:56,034 --> 00:17:59,034
I'm sorry, you guys. I can't this time.

212
00:17:59,034 --> 00:18:02,034
I have to trust and focus on what Asuri and Kurada are doing.

213
00:18:02,034 --> 00:18:05,034
I don't know why. I can't explain it.

214
00:18:05,034 --> 00:18:09,034
But there's a loud voice in my head telling me this is what I have to do.

215
00:18:09,034 --> 00:18:16,034
Oh. Okay. I see it now.

216
00:18:16,034 --> 00:18:18,034
Those three players keep looking at each other.

217
00:18:19,034 --> 00:18:22,034
Which means they're communicating strategy with their eyes.

218
00:18:25,034 --> 00:18:26,034
Take the shot, Aoi!

219
00:18:27,034 --> 00:18:30,034
I can do a middle range shot right now!

220
00:18:30,034 --> 00:18:31,034
No!

221
00:18:47,034 --> 00:18:48,034
Way to go, guys!

222
00:18:49,034 --> 00:18:51,034
That's how you break them up, Aoi! Brilliant!

223
00:18:52,034 --> 00:18:53,034
One goal down!

224
00:18:53,034 --> 00:18:54,034
Hey, I'm not worried about it.

225
00:18:55,034 --> 00:18:56,034
We're still up by two goals!

226
00:18:57,034 --> 00:18:58,034
Fifteen more minutes!

227
00:18:58,034 --> 00:18:59,034
Keep it up and we win!

228
00:19:00,034 --> 00:19:03,034
Not worried? I don't know about that.

229
00:19:03,034 --> 00:19:05,034
I gotta admit, I didn't even see it coming.

230
00:19:06,034 --> 00:19:08,034
There's so many of us on defense.

231
00:19:08,034 --> 00:19:10,034
Yet they managed to break us up effortlessly.

232
00:19:11,034 --> 00:19:12,034
There are only three of them.

233
00:19:13,034 --> 00:19:15,034
Gotta get going! Move!

234
00:19:16,034 --> 00:19:18,034
That was your shot.

235
00:19:19,034 --> 00:19:21,034
Why did you pass the ball to me?

236
00:19:22,034 --> 00:19:24,034
I'm not sure myself.

237
00:19:25,034 --> 00:19:26,034
Hmm.

238
00:19:31,034 --> 00:19:34,034
He was right. That was my shot.

239
00:19:35,034 --> 00:19:39,034
I didn't even realize I was doing it.

240
00:19:40,034 --> 00:19:41,034
I passed the ball to Asuri.

241
00:19:42,034 --> 00:19:45,034
Normally, I would have gone for the goal myself. No question.

242
00:19:46,034 --> 00:19:47,034
But I couldn't.

243
00:19:48,034 --> 00:19:50,034
I didn't want to compromise my pride as a forward.

244
00:19:50,034 --> 00:19:52,034
So then, why did I?

245
00:19:53,034 --> 00:19:54,034
Uh-huh?

246
00:20:01,034 --> 00:20:02,034
That's right.

247
00:20:03,034 --> 00:20:04,034
Help me!

248
00:20:04,034 --> 00:20:05,034
Teach me how to play soccer!

249
00:20:06,034 --> 00:20:07,034
Your way!

250
00:20:07,034 --> 00:20:12,034
You came here to make a change in yourself, didn't you?

251
00:20:13,034 --> 00:20:16,034
I get it! It's finally happening!

252
00:20:17,034 --> 00:20:18,034
I'm learning how to play soccer!

253
00:20:19,034 --> 00:20:20,034
Ashito!

254
00:20:21,034 --> 00:20:23,034
Watch out! They're coming in from the side!

255
00:20:29,034 --> 00:20:30,034
You know, you were right.

256
00:20:31,034 --> 00:20:33,034
Something interesting is happening with those three fellas.

257
00:20:34,034 --> 00:20:35,034
They're making eye contact.

258
00:20:36,034 --> 00:20:38,034
Like constantly looking back and forth at each other.

259
00:20:39,034 --> 00:20:40,034
Trying to communicate.

260
00:20:41,034 --> 00:20:43,034
In sports like soccer, where the situations can change,

261
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:47,034
you don't have the time or space to yell out instructions to your teammates.

262
00:20:48,034 --> 00:20:49,034
In which case, the most effective method is...

263
00:20:50,034 --> 00:20:51,034
using eye contact.

264
00:20:52,034 --> 00:20:55,034
When Oof Tanz became the general manager for the national team,

265
00:20:56,034 --> 00:20:59,034
he made sure to ingrain the most basic of basics into his players.

266
00:21:00,034 --> 00:21:04,034
And yet, even today's top players haven't been able to master it.

267
00:21:05,034 --> 00:21:07,034
Magic just doesn't happen by glancing at each other.

268
00:21:07,034 --> 00:21:08,034
Huh?

269
00:21:09,034 --> 00:21:11,034
There needs to be a mutual understanding between the players.

270
00:21:12,034 --> 00:21:14,034
And if that's the case here,

271
00:21:14,034 --> 00:21:17,034
then I'd say those three have an ideal relationship.

272
00:21:23,034 --> 00:21:25,034
Asuri! I need you to run in!

273
00:21:28,034 --> 00:21:29,034
Okay!

274
00:21:30,034 --> 00:21:31,034
Oh no you don't!

275
00:21:31,034 --> 00:21:38,034
It's all coming to me now.

276
00:21:39,034 --> 00:21:40,034
Three!

277
00:21:41,034 --> 00:21:43,034
That's the number that really matters out here.

278
00:21:44,034 --> 00:21:46,034
Not one, or two, but three.

279
00:21:47,034 --> 00:21:51,034
Soccer is a sport where you need three teammates to carry the ball forward together.

280
00:21:52,034 --> 00:21:54,034
The most intriguing part for me is...

281
00:21:55,034 --> 00:21:57,034
What happened to make them bond so suddenly?

282
00:22:00,034 --> 00:22:01,034
This is so exciting!

283
00:22:02,034 --> 00:22:03,034
Takurada!

284
00:22:06,034 --> 00:22:08,034
No matter how tight the defense might be,

285
00:22:09,034 --> 00:22:11,034
when three people who share the same mind go at it,

286
00:22:12,034 --> 00:22:13,034
they will create a gap!

287
00:22:13,034 --> 00:22:14,034
Yeah!

288
00:22:17,034 --> 00:22:18,034
Yeah!

289
00:22:19,034 --> 00:22:20,034
Yeah!

290
00:22:20,034 --> 00:22:21,034
Yeah!

291
00:22:25,034 --> 00:22:26,034
Ha ha!

292
00:22:27,034 --> 00:22:28,034
Huh?

293
00:22:30,034 --> 00:22:31,034
Oh!

294
00:22:31,034 --> 00:23:01,014
Thank you.

295
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,186
Next time on Awashi, Eagle Eye.

